          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            A
            %strong Sullivan model
            of a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+space"} rational space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            is a particularly well-behaved commutative
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphic
            to the dg-algebra of Sullivan forms on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %em Sullivan algebras
            are precisely the cofibrant objects in the standard
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on dg-algebras
          %p
            Sullivan models are a central tool in
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
            Sullivan models are particularly well-behaved
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebras"} differential graded-commutative algebras
            that are equivalent to the dg-algebras of
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "differential+forms+on+simplices#PiecewisePolynomialDifferentialForms"} piecewise polynomial differential forms on topological spaces
            %em minimal
            Sullivan algebras provide convenient representatives that correspond bijectively to rational homotopy types under this correspondence.
          %p
            Abstractly, (relative) Sullivan models are the (relative)
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cell+complexes"} cell complexes
            in the standard
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on dg-algebras
          %p We now describe this in detail. First some notation and preliminaries:
          #FiniteType.num_defn
            %h6#definition_2 Definition
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/of+finite+type"}> of finite type
                )
            %ul
              %li
                %p
                  A
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                  is
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/of+finite+type"} of finite type
                  if in each degree it is finite dimensional. In this case we write
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mi V
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^*
                  for its degreewise dual.
              %li
                %p
                  A
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
                  is
                  %em
                    %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/of+finite+type"} of finite type
                  if it is the Grassmann algebra
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ∧
                          %mo •
                        %msup
                          %mi V
                          %mo *
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet V^*
                  on a graded vector space of finite type
                %p (the dualization here is just convention, that will help make some of the following constructions come out nicely).
              %li
                %p
                  A
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/CW-complex"} CW-complex
                  is of finite type if it is built out of finitely many cells in each degree.
          %p
            For
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            a
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℕ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
            write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo ∧
                    %mo •
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \wedge^\bullet V
            for the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
            over it. Equipped with the trivial differential
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi d
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d = 0
            this is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dgc-algebra"} semifree dgc-algebra
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wedge^\bullet V, d=0)
          %p
            With
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            our ground
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
            we write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %mo ,
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k,0)
            for the corresponding
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"} dg-algebra
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal structure
            on
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi dgAlg
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Grassmann+algebra"} Grassmann algebra
            on the 0-vector space
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k,0) = (\wedge^\bullet 0, 0)
          #SullivanAlgebra.num_defn
            %h6#definition_3 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Sullivan algebras)
            %p
              A
              %strong relatived Sullivan algebra
              is a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homomorphism"} homomorphism
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+graded-commutative+algebras"} differential graded-commutative algebras
              that is an inclusion of the form
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %msub
                      %mo ⊗
                      %mi k
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo ′
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (A,d) \hookrightarrow (A \otimes_k \wedge^\bullet V, d')
            %p
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi A
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (A,d)
              any
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dgc-algebra"} dgc-algebra
              and for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              some
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/graded+vector+space"} graded vector space
            %ol
              %li
                %p
                  there is a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/well+ordered+set"} well ordered set
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi J
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} J
                  indexing a
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/linear+basis"} linear basis
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi α
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi V
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi α
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi J
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \{v_\alpha \in V| \alpha \in J\}
                  of
                  = succeed ";" do
                    %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                      %semantics
                        %mrow
                          %mi V
                        %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              %li
                %p
                  writing
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi V
                          %mrow
                            %mo &lt;
                            %mi β
                        %mo ≔
                        %mi span
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi α
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                        %mi α
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi β
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_{\lt \beta} \coloneqq span(v_\alpha | \alpha \lt \beta)
                  then for all basis elements
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi β
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_\beta
                  we have that
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi d
                    %mo ′
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi β
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                    %mo ⊗
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi β
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    d' v_\beta \in A \otimes \wedge^\bullet V_{\lt \beta}
                    \\,.
            %p
              This is called a
              %strong minimal
              relative Sullivan algebra if in addition the condition
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi α
                    %mo &lt;
                    %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⇒
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi deg
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi α
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi deg
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi β
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\alpha \lt \beta) \Rightarrow (deg v_\alpha  \leq deg v_\beta)
            %p
              holds. For a Sullivan algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k,0) \to (\wedge^\bullet V, d)
              relative to the tensor unit we call the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dgc-algebra"} semifree dgc-algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wedge^\bullet V,d)
              simply a
              = succeed "," do
                %strong Sullivan algebra
              %strong minimal Sullivan algebra
              if
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k,0) \to (\wedge^\bullet V, d)
              is a minimal relative Sullivan algebra.
          %p
            (e.g.
            = succeed ")" do
              %a{:href => "#Hess06"} Hess 06, def. 1.10, remark 1.11
          %p
            See also the section
            %a{:href => "model+structure+on+dg-algebras#SullivanAlgebras"} Sullivan algebras
            at
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on dg-algebras
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark Remark
            %p
              The special condition on the ordering in the relative Sullivan algebra says that these morphisms are composites of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/pushouts"} pushouts
              of the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cofibrantly+generated+model+category"} generating cofibrations
              for the
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+structure+on+dg-algebras"} model structure on dg-algebras
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ↪
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo ,
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S(n) \hookrightarrow D(n)
                    \\,,
            %p where
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi S
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    S(n) = (\wedge^\bullet \langle c \rangle, d = 0)
            %p
              is the dg-algebra on a single generator in degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              with vanishing differential, and where
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                    %mi c
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mi b
                    %mo =
                    %mi c
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mi c
                    %mo =
                    %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    D(n) = (\wedge^\bullet (\langle b \rangle \oplus \langle c \rangle), d b = c, d c = 0)
            %p
              with
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              an additional generator in degree
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n-1
            %p
              Therefore for
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi A
                      %mo ∈
                      %mi dgcAlg
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A \in dgcAlg
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mtable
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi S
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mover
                              %mo →
                              %mi ϕ
                          %mtd
                            %mi A
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                          %mtd
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ↓
                        %mtr
                          %mtd
                            %mi D
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi n
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mtd
                            %mo →
                          %mtd
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                            %mi A
                            %mo ⊗
                            %msup
                              %mo ∧
                              %mo •
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                            %mi b
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                            %mo ,
                            %mi d
                            %mi b
                            %mo =
                            %mi ϕ
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\array{
                    S(n) &amp;\stackrel{\phi}{\to}&amp; A
                    \\\
                    \\downarrow &amp;&amp; \downarrow
                    \\\
                    D(n) &amp;\to&amp; (A \otimes \wedge^ \bullet \langle b \rangle, d b = \phi)
                    }
            %p
              is precisely a choice
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ϕ
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \phi \in A
              of a
              = succeed "-closed" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi d
                        %mi A
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d_A
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
              and results in adjoining to
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
              the element
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi b
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} b
              whose differential is
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi d
                      %mi b
                      %mo =
                      %mi ϕ
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} d b = \phi
            %p
              Notice that it follows in particular that the cofibrations in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi dgAlg
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dgAlg_{proj}
              are precisely all the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
              of relative Sullivan algebra inclusions.
          .num_remark
            %h6#remark_2 Remark
            %p
              %strong
                (
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi L
                        %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} L_\infty
                \-algebras)
            %p
              Because they are
              = succeed "s," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/semifree+dga"} semifree dga
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi d
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wedge^\bullet V,d)
              are (at least for degreewise finite dimensional
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi V
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              = succeed "s" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Chevalley-Eilenberg+algebra"} Chevalley-Eilenberg algebra
              = succeed "s." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E-algebra"} L-∞-algebra
            %p
              The co-commutative differential co-algebra encoding the corresponding
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/L-%E2%88%9E-algebra"} L-∞-algebra
              is the free cocommutative algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mo ∨
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \vee^\bullet V^*
              on the degreewise dual of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
              with differential
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi D
                      %mo =
                      %msup
                        %mi d
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} D = d^*
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi D
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ∨
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ∨
                    %mi ⋯
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi d
                    %mi ω
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 1
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mn 2
                    %mo ,
                    %mi ⋯
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi v
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\omega(D(v_1 \vee v_2 \vee \cdots v_n)) =
                    \- (d \omega) (v_1, v_2, \cdots,  v_n)
            %p
              for all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ω
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \omega \in V
              and all
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi i
                      %mo ∈
                      %msup
                        %mi V
                        %mo *
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \in V^*
          .num_defn
            %h6#definition_4 Definition
            %p
              %strong (Sullivan models)
            %p
              For
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simply+connected"} simply connected
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/topological+space"} topological space
              = succeed "," do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %strong Sullivan (minimal) model
              for
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              is a Sullivan (minimal) algebra
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wedge^\bullet V^\ast, d_V)
              equipped with a
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quasi-isomorphism"} quasi-isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo ⟶
                      %mo ≃
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi pwpoly
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (\wedge^\bullet V^*, d_V)
                    \\stackrel{\simeq}{\longrightarrow}
                    \\Omega^\bullet_{pwpoly}(X)
            %p
              to the dg-algebra of
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/piecewise+polynomial+differential+forms"} piecewise polynomial differential forms
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#as_cofibrations As cofibrations
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition Proposition
            %p
              %strong (cofibrations are relative Sullivan algebras)
            %p
              The cofibrations in the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/projective+model+structure+on+differential+graded-commutative+algebras"} projective model structure on differential graded-commutative algebras
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgcAlg_{\mathbb{N}})_{proj}
              are precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
              of relative Sullivan algebra inclusions (def.
              = succeed ")." do
                %a.maruku-ref{:href => "#SullivanAlgebra"}
            %p
              Accordingly, the cofibrant objects in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mi ℕ
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi proj
                    %mrow
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (dgcAlg_{\mathbb{N}})_proj{}
              are precisely the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/retracts"} retracts
              of Sullivan algebras.
          .num_prop
            %h6#proposition_2 Proposition
            %p
              Minimal Sullivan models are unique up to
              = succeed "." do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
          %p
            e.g
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Hess06"} Hess 06, prop 1.18
          %h3#rationalization Rationalization
          #SullivanRationalizationEquivalence.num_theorem
            %h6#theorem Theorem
            %p
              Consider the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction"} derived adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi Top
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi sSet
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℝ
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi poly
                            %mo •
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝕃
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mi poly
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ho(Top)
                    \\simeq
                    Ho(sSet)
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{\mathbb{R} \Omega^\bullet_{poly}}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\mathbb{L} K_{poly} }{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    Ho( (dgcAlg_{\mathbb{Q}, \geq 0})^{op} )
            %p
              induced from the of the
              = succeed "-" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/PL+de+Rham+complex"} PL de Rham complex
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Quillen+adjunction"} Quillen adjunction
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msub
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mo
                      %mi proj
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %munderover
                      %mo ⊥
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mi poly
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi poly
                            %mo •
                    %msub
                      %mi sSet
                      %mi Quillen
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    (dgcAlg_{\mathbb{Q}, \geq 0}_{proj})^{op}
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{K_{poly}}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\Omega^\bullet_{poly}}{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\bot}
                    sSet_{Quillen}
            %p
              (
              %a{:href => "rational+homotopy+theory#SullivanRationalizationAdjunction"}> this theorem
              ).
            %p
              Then: On the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/full+subcategory"} full subcategory
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mo ,
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                      %mi fin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Ho(Top_{\mathbb{Q}, \geq 1}^{fin})
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/nilpotent+topological+space"} nilpotent
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+topological+spaces"} rational topological spaces
              of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/finite+type"} finite type
              this adjunction restricts to an
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/equivalence+of+categories"} equivalence of categories
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Top
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mo ,
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 1
                      %mi fin
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munderover
                      %mo ≃
                      %munder
                        %mo ⟶
                        %mrow
                          %mi ℝ
                          %msubsup
                            %mi Ω
                            %mi poly
                            %mo •
                      %mover
                        %mo ⟵
                        %mrow
                          %mi 𝕃
                          %msub
                            %mi K
                            %mi poly
                    %mi Ho
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi dgcAlg
                      %mrow
                        %mi ℚ
                        %mo ,
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 1
                      %mi fin
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi op
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo .
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    Ho(Top_{\mathbb{Q}, \gt 1}^{fin})
                    \\underoverset
                    {\underset{\mathbb{R} \Omega^\bullet_{poly}}{\longrightarrow}}
                    {\overset{\mathbb{L} K_{poly} }{\longleftarrow}}
                    {\simeq}
                    Ho( (dgcAlg_{\mathbb{Q}, \gt 1}^{fin})^{op} )
                    \\,.
            %p
              In particular the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/derived+adjunction+unit"} derived adjunction unit
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo ⟶
                    %msub
                      %mi K
                      %mi poly
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Ω
                      %mi pwpoly
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X \longrightarrow K_{poly}(\Omega^\bullet_{pwpoly}(X))
            %p
              exhibits the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rationalization"} rationalization
              of
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
          %p
            This is the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fundamental+theorem+of+dgc-algebraic+rational+homotopy+theory"} fundamental theorem of dgc-algebraic rational homotopy theory
          %p
            It follows that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cochain+cohomology"} cochain cohomology
            of the cochain complex of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/piecewise+polynomial+differential+forms"} piecewise polynomial differential forms
            on any topological, hence equivalently that of any of its
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sullivan+models"} Sullivan models
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ordinary+cohomology"} ordinary cohomology
            with coefficients in the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+numbers"} rational numbers
          .num_theorem
            %h6#theorem_2 Theorem
            %p
              Let
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mo ∧
                      %mo •
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mo *
                    %mo ,
                    %msub
                      %mi d
                      %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\wedge^\bullet V^*, d_V)
              be a minimal Sullivan model of a simply connected rational topological space
              = succeed "." do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi X
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/isomorphism"} isomorphism
            .maruku-equation
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi π
                      %mo •
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    \\pi_\bullet(X)
                    \\simeq
                    V
            %p
              between the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups"} homotopy groups
              of
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              and the generators of the minimal Sullivan model.
          %p
            e.g.
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#Hess06"} Hess 06, theorem 1.24
          %h3#relation_to_nilpotent_algebras
            Relation to nilpotent
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
